6) Output concise review before commits
Print a compact table/list:
- bundle id
- file count
- commit subject
- 1-line summary
- confidence

7) Commit phase
If mode="plan":
- Output only ordered, idempotent commands for each bundle (POSIX first + `# pwsh` alternates if needed).
- Do not mutate repo.

If mode="execute":
- Stage only selected files per bundle.
- Create one commit per bundle in dependency order.
- After each commit, output: `<hash> - <subject>`.
- Include rollback snippet under `post_commit_checks`.

8) Final report
Return:
- total_commits_created
- ordered_commits: `<hash> - <subject>`
- per-commit 1-line summary
- confirmation that `main` branch was used and no new branch was created.

Advanced Repo Rules:
- Submodules: check `git submodule status`; stage only pointer updates when required.
- LFS: avoid binary rebuild churn; verify tracked patterns if relevant.
- Codegen: include generated files only when feature requires regeneration; otherwise exclude generated blobs with reason.
- Worktrees: ensure commands target active worktree only.

Non-Goals:
- No release tagging/version bump/changelog/CI rewrites unless explicitly part of change intent.
